## SQ-TP-01
@group A
@commands boot with the donor present; second boot with `tempad_upstream/` renamed away
@pass first boot reaches `Done (`, no `tempad` errors in latest.log, `/datapack list` shows `tempad_upstream_data`; second boot stops with a message naming `tempad_upstream/` and the jar
@fails translator or pack registration (`forge/UpstreamTranslator`, `BuiltInPacks.addUpstream`); donor sha1 mismatch
@reviewed 2026-11-16
bootexpect Done \(
shell grep -hiE "tempad" logs/latest.log | grep -iE "error|exception|fail" | head -20; echo "errlines=$(grep -hiE 'tempad' logs/latest.log | grep -ciE 'error|exception|fail')"
> datapack list
sleep 2
expect tempad_upstream
look shell output errlines=0 (no tempad error lines); the second boot (tempad_upstream/ renamed away) is its own boot: its latest.log must stop with a message naming tempad_upstream/ and the jar
## SQ-TP-02 | phase 1 recipes, forge tags, new-location upgrade absent
@group A
@commands `/cdevtest rdetail tempad:tempad`, the same for `chronon_cell`, `chronon_battery`, `chronon_generator`, `chronometer`, `time_steel_shaped`; `/cdevtest rdetail tempad:upgrades/new_location`
@pass each recipe loads with `forge:` tags (ender pearls, quartz, tinted glass); the new-location upgrade recipe is absent while `require_location_upgrade=false`
@fails c: -> forge: tag map in the translator; condition `tempad:required_location_upgrade`
@from batches/r1107tp/a1.qb
@reviewed 2026-11-16
> cdevtest rdetail tempad:
waitlog verb=rdetail done=1 60
expect tempad:tempad
expect tempad:chronon_cell
expect tempad:chronon_battery
expect tempad:chronon_generator
expect tempad:chronometer
expect tempad:time_steel_shaped
reject upgrades/new_location
shell grep -hE "verb=rdetail id=tempad:(tempad|chronon_cell|chronon_battery|chronon_generator|chronometer|time_steel_shaped) " logs/latest.log | head -60
look inputs use forge: tags (ender pearls, quartz, tinted glass) or items; no c: tags
reject verb=\S+ .*done=0

## SQ-TP-04
@group A
@commands Teleport to the saved location in the same dimension and in the Nether; check chronons before and after; use again at once
@pass a timedoor opens, costs 1000 chronons, carries the player; the door closes after 200 ticks (an API open starts the 40-tick Tempad cooldown, owner ruling 2026-11-18, reversing ruling 6; `[ztp] cd true` right after the open)
@fails `TimedoorEntity`, `forge/Teleports`
@reviewed 2026-11-18
# makes the three locations later TP rows use (Home One, Far East, Hell Spot); bot qa holds the Tempad in slot 0
> forceload add -16 -16 48 16
> execute in minecraft:the_nether run forceload add -16 -16 16 16
> execute in minecraft:the_nether run fill -3 119 -3 3 119 3 minecraft:obsidian
> execute in minecraft:the_nether run fill -3 120 -3 3 123 3 minecraft:air
> pbot spawn qa 0.5 -60 0.5 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 3
> clear qa
> item replace entity qa hotbar.0 with tempad:tempad
> ztp setchr qa 0 6000
> ztp save qa Home One
> tp qa 30.5 -60 0.5 0 0
> ztp save qa Far East
> execute in minecraft:the_nether run tp qa 0.5 120 0.5 0 0
sleep 2
> ztp save qa Hell Spot
> execute in minecraft:overworld run tp qa 0.5 -60 0.5 0 0
sleep 2
> ztp locs qa
waitlog \[ztp\] locs total 20
expect \[ztp\] loc tempad:default .* "Home One" minecraft:overworld 0\.50 -60\.00 0\.50
expect \[ztp\] loc tempad:default .* "Far East" minecraft:overworld 30\.50
expect \[ztp\] loc tempad:default .* "Hell Spot" minecraft:the_nether 0\.50 120\.00
> kill @e[type=tempad:timedoor]
> ztp open qa tempad:default Far East
waitlog \[ztp\] open .*Far 20
expect \[ztp\] open .*"Far East".* -> message none chronons 6000 -> 5000
# owner ruling 6 reversed (2026-11-18): an API open sets the cooldown (TimedoorEntity.openTimedoor adds 40 ticks for non-creative players); SQ-TP-41 checks the macro path
> ztp cd qa
waitlog \[ztp\] cd 20
expect \[ztp\] cd true percent [1-9]
> ztp doors
waitlog \[ztp\] doors total 20
expect \[ztp\] door minecraft:overworld .* target minecraft:overworld \(30\.5, -60\.0, 0\.5\)
> pbot look qa 0 0
# judge-12, 2026-11-18: a 100-tick walk carried the bot through the door and 12 blocks back west (x 17.7); 20 ticks ends just past the exit
> pbot moveto qa 0.5 6 walk 20
waitlog verb=pbot\.moveto bot=qa end= 20
> cdevtest player qa
expect verb=player name=qa dim=minecraft:overworld x=(2\d|3\d)(\.\d+)?\b
> cdevtest tickwarp 220
waitlog verb=tickwarp end=done 30
> ztp doors
waitlog \[ztp\] doors total 20
expect \[ztp\] doors total 0
> ztp setchr qa 0 6000
> ztp open qa tempad:default Hell Spot
waitlog \[ztp\] open .*Hell 20
expect \[ztp\] open .*"Hell Spot".* -> message none chronons 6000 -> 5000
> ztp doors
waitlog \[ztp\] doors total 20
expect \[ztp\] door minecraft:overworld .* target minecraft:the_nether
> kill @e[type=tempad:timedoor]
reject \[ztp\] (error|unknown subcommand)
reject verb=\S+ .*done=0
look the bot walked through the Far East door (player x near 30.5)

