## SQ-TP-41 | the Tempad macro (item use path) opens a door and starts the 40-tick cooldown; a second use during it opens nothing
@group A
@commands Bot with a Tempad and 6000 chronons saves a location, pins it, sets the pinned-location macro; `/ztp macro` twice at once, then again after 45 ticks
@pass first macro: a door to the pinned location, `[ztp] cd true`; second macro at once: still one door; after the cooldown: a second door (API opens through `/ztp open` also start the cooldown, owner ruling 2026-11-18, SQ-TP-04)
@fails no cooldown: the macro path does not call the item cooldown (`UseMacroPacket` handler); a second door at once: the cooldown is not checked
@reviewed 2026-11-18
# owner ruling 6 reversed (2026-11-18): both paths start the cooldown; this row checks the macro path (the item-use path a player's shift-use takes)
> forceload add -16 -16 48 16
> pbot spawn t40 0.5 -60 4.5 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 3
> clear t40
> item replace entity t40 hotbar.0 with tempad:tempad
> ztp setchr t40 0 6000
> tp t40 30.5 -60 4.5 0 0
> ztp save t40 Cool Spot
> tp t40 0.5 -60 4.5 0 0
sleep 2
> ztp pin t40 tempad:default Cool Spot
> ztp settings t40 tempad:teleport tempad:pinned_location
> kill @e[type=tempad:timedoor]
sleep 2
> ztp macro t40
> ztp cd t40
waitlog \[ztp\] cd 20
expect \[ztp\] cd true
> ztp macro t40
> ztp doors
waitlog \[ztp\] doors total 20
expect \[ztp\] doors total 1\b
> cdevtest tickwarp 45
waitlog verb=tickwarp end=done 30
> kill @e[type=tempad:timedoor]
> ztp macro t40
> ztp doors
count \[ztp\] door minecraft:overworld .* target minecraft:overworld \(30\.5, -60\.0, 4\.5\) >= 2
> kill @e[type=tempad:timedoor]
> pbot remove t40
reject \[ztp\] (error|unknown subcommand)
reject verb=\S+ .*done=0
look the macro reply lines; the pinned id in the settings reply
