## CQ-TP-17 | Timeline app shows the in-world day and clock (A5)
@group client
@commands Survival client: hold a Tempad, walk more than 8 blocks twice (logs two wandering entries), sleep through a night, walk again; open the Timeline app; compare with the clock in the Tempad's title bar; relog and open it again
@pass each new entry's last line reads `Day N, HH:MM` (day 1 = the first day; the hours match the title bar clock at the time it was logged; the entry after sleeping has a higher day); no real-world date on new entries; entries survive a relog; entries from a save before the fix still show their real-world date
@fails a real date on a new entry: `HistoricalLocation.dayTime` not recorded (`TravelHistoryAttachment.logLocation`) or not sent (`write` / `read` must both carry the long); a disconnect opening the app: the packet order of `HistoricalLocation.write` and `read` differs
@draft no batch holds this row yet; needs a client

